\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{From quarter averages to half averages}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{In one dimension let #{N=4M}. The [box mean map](fdip-01D5)
with #{B=4} averages each consecutive group of #{M} sites.
If these 4 averages are #{z(0),z(1),z(2),z(3)}, the
[merging map](fdip-01D5) to #{B'=2} gives
##{M_{2,4}z=\left(\frac{z(0)+z(1)}2,
\frac{z(2)+z(3)}2\right).}
Each entry is the direct average over the corresponding #{2M}
sites, because the two groups have equal size. Averaging the
two resulting entries gives #{\tfrac14\sum_{b=0}^3z(b)},
the mean over the whole cycle. The equal weights express the
equal number of fine sites in each part.}
